From: PyDevices audiodsp
Date: Mon, 25 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] src/assembly.h: keep mingw-w64 GCC off the MSVC-only branch

Purpose: assembly.h guards its MSVC-only inline-`__asm{}` branch (and an
MSVC-only `#pragma warning`) on `defined _WIN32`, which mingw-w64 GCC --
this workspace's Windows MicroPython target -- also defines. Excluding
`__GNUC__` makes mingw fall through to the portable C fallback at the
bottom of the file, the same one the unix build already uses. Upstream
never hits this: CircuitPython has no Windows port, so the branch was
only ever reached by real MSVC.

Provenance: written for the audiodsp Windows MicroPython port (originally
carried in the parent workspace's own patches/adafruit_mp3; ownership
moved here in Phase 2 of the modernization program). Full rationale:
docs/upstream-diff.md in
the audiodsp repository, "Tier 5 audiomp3: three Windows-only local
fixes, no unix impact".
Upstream-version: authored against Adafruit_MP3
aac02afd9f24d2ee930f650156654ab9211a306a, the exact commit
CircuitPython 10.2.1 vendors (see DEPENDENCIES.lock).
Order: first and only patch in the series. Applied by
scripts/fetch_deps.sh on top of the pinned commit.
Test: build the Windows MicroPython port (mingw-w64) with the audiodsp
usermod; the unix build is unaffected because it never entered this
branch.

diff --git a/src/assembly.h b/src/assembly.h
index 7c714cd..f5ca2e2 100644
--- a/src/assembly.h
+++ b/src/assembly.h
@@ -60,7 +60,17 @@
 extern "C" {
 #endif
 
-#if (defined _WIN32 && !defined _WIN32_WCE) || (defined __WINS__ && defined _SYMBIAN) || defined(_OPENWAVE_SIMULATOR) || defined(WINCE_EMULATOR)    /* Symbian emulator for Ix86 */
+/* PyDevices local patch (see docs/upstream-diff.md in the audiodsp repo,
+ * "Tier 5 audiomp3"): added `&& !defined(__GNUC__)` to this branch's
+ * condition. It guards MSVC-only `__asm { ... }` intrinsic syntax and an
+ * MSVC-only `#pragma warning`, neither of which mingw-w64 GCC accepts, but
+ * mingw-w64 GCC (this workspace's Windows MicroPython target) also defines
+ * `_WIN32`. Upstream never hits this: CircuitPython has no Windows port, so
+ * this branch was only ever reached by real MSVC. Excluding __GNUC__ falls
+ * through to the portable C fallback near the bottom of this file (the same
+ * one this workspace's unix build already uses), not to a different branch.
+ */
+#if (defined _WIN32 && !defined _WIN32_WCE && !defined(__GNUC__)) || (defined __WINS__ && defined _SYMBIAN) || defined(_OPENWAVE_SIMULATOR) || defined(WINCE_EMULATOR)    /* Symbian emulator for Ix86 */
 
 #pragma warning( disable : 4035 )	/* complains about inline asm not returning a value */
 
